# ============================================================
# FireGuard Capsule™ - Environment Configuration Example
# ============================================================
#
# Public-safe configuration template.
# Do not place passwords, API keys, tokens, private keys,
# or other secrets in this file.
#
# The current FireGuard backend does not load a .env file.
# This file documents the environment configuration currently
# used by the Flutter application and local development workflow.
# ============================================================


# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Flutter API Base URL
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Local FastAPI server.
FIREGUARD_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Android emulator:
# FIREGUARD_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000

# Physical device on the same LAN:
# FIREGUARD_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.100:8000


# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Important
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# The current backend configuration is intentionally simple:
#
# - SQLite database location is defined by the backend.
# - NASA FIRMS intelligence currently uses local project data.
# - The backend does not currently load environment variables
#   through python-dotenv or a Settings/BaseSettings system.
#
# Future production deployments may introduce environment-based
# configuration for databases, secrets, external services, and
# deployment-specific settings.
#
# Never commit:
# - passwords
# - API keys
# - device tokens
# - private keys
# - production database credentials
# - other confidential deployment secrets
#
# ============================================================
